      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With exactly 3 mana available (Golgari Rot Farm produces BG, Forest produces G), casting Squirrel Nest costs 1GG and uses all mana. Chitterspitter costs 2G and also uses all mana. Both are reasonable turn 3 plays. However, Squirrel Nest enchants a land and ties its token production to that land's tap ability, meaning it competes with mana production. Chitterspitter produces tokens without tapping a land, and has the acorn counter scaling mechanic. Additionally, the player has Swamp in hand as their land drop next turn - casting Chitterspitter now and playing Swamp next turn would leave them with 4 mana (BBGG) and the ability to make squirrel tokens without sacrificing mana production. With Squirrel Nest, enchanting Forest means tapping Forest for a token instead of mana. That said, Squirrel Nest on Golgari Rot Farm (which produces BG) would be suboptimal since you'd lose 2 mana for a token. On Forest it's only 1 mana lost. The choice between these two 3-drops is close enough to be debatable, but Chitterspitter is generally considered the stronger card since it doesn't cost you mana production and scales better over time.",
