      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem25P Lucky chose Rekindling Phoenix from the Maestros Charm top-5 look, but their mana base currently produces U, B, and colorless (Path of Ancestry for commander colors U/B/R, Swamp, Island, Arcane Signet, Fellwar Stone). They have no red source on board yet, and Rekindling Phoenix costs {2}{R}{R} requiring double red. Meanwhile, Cascade Bluffs was among the choices — a land that can produce {R}{R} — which would directly fix the mana problem and enable casting both Rekindling Phoenix later (if drawn) and Cryptic Pursuit (which needs U and R) already in hand. Alternatively, Waste Management is a strong instant-speed removal/graveyard hate spell castable with current mana. Taking a double-red creature when you have zero red sources and a red-producing land in the same pile is a sequencing error that may strand the Phoenix in hand for multiple turns.",
