    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Gem25P Lucky cast Sinister Concierge (a 2/1 for 1U) instead of Cryptic Pursuit (2UR enchantment) when they had the mana for either. Sinister Concierge is a fragile 2/1 whose main value is its death trigger to exile a creature with suspend. However, the player already has Rekindling Phoenix (summoning sick) as a creature, and casting Cryptic Pursuit would set up an engine that generates value every time they cast instants/sorceries from hand (manifesting cards) and recovers instants/sorceries from face-down creatures that die. With Anhelo as commander (casualty 2 synergy), Cryptic Pursuit would be a powerful engine piece. Additionally, casting the Concierge before combat (when there's nothing to attack into profitably anyway) is fine, but prioritizing the enchantment engine over a small creature seems better long-term. The Concierge could also be cast later when there's a better target for its death trigger. That said, deploying a creature that can serve as a casualty 2 sacrifice for Anhelo later has some merit.",
